==Trivia==
*"Koronium" is a wordplay of [[Kory]] and the hypothetical chemical substance [[wikipedia:Coronium|Coronium]], later discovered to be ionized iron.
*He appears to be wearing the infamous [[wikia:kyojin-no-hoshi:Dai League Ball Training Cast|Dai League Ball Training Cast]] from the classic baseball manga [[wikipedia:Star of the Giants|''Star of the Giants'']]. In the story, the main protagonist [[wikia:kyojin-no-hoshi:Hyūma Hoshi|Hyūma Hoshi]] is forced to wear this spring-loaded device for 24 hours as part of his sadistic training by his abusive father [[wikia:kyojin-no-hoshi:Ittetsu Hoshi|Ittetsu]]. His Japanese description saying he is feared an "oni kyōkan" or "demon teacher" (鬼教官) refers to how Ittetsu gets called an ''[[wikipedia:Oni|oni]]'' by one of his trainees, [[wikia:kyojin-no-hoshi:Chūta Ban|Chūta Ban]]. The irony is that Koronium is a base coach, not a player, meaning he should be the one making others wear the training cast.
**The reason why Ittetsu is referenced by a [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemy may be that the ''tetsu'' (徹) part of his name sounds exactly like 鉄, meaning iron.
**Incidentally, ''Star of the Giants'' and Hyūma Hoshi are also referenced by the Japanese name and description of another baseball-themed enemy, [[Hackey]], which may imply a connection between him and Koronium.
*The "NLB" mentioned in his description is a reference to MLB, or Major League Baseball. The "N" presumably stands for ''neko'', the Japanese word for cat.
*[[Lakeside Bootcamp]], the stage Koronium is introduced in, is likely a reference to his harsh nature during training.
*[[Three Evil Brothers]] implies that Koronium, Kory and [[Berserkory]] are brothers.
**This also implies that [[Deathkory]] is not related, although this can be attributed to DeathKory being added after the stage was made.

